    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **283 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city title-casing and reuse behaviour for owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Added `owner.setCity(resolveCity(owner.getCity()))` before persisting, so the stored/returned `city` follows the new rule.\n- `resolveCity(String city)` \u2014 scans existing owners for one whose city matches case-insensitively; if found, reuses that owner's **exact spelling**; otherwise falls back to title-casing.\n- `titleCase(String city)` \u2014 upper-cases the first letter of each whitespace-separated word and lower-cases the rest, preserving original spacing (e.g. `\"gOtHaM cITY\"` \u2192 `\"Gotham City\"`).\n\nBecause the resolved city is set before `nextCustomerCode(...)`, the existing case-insensitive customer-code logic is unaffected.\n\n**New tests** (`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`):\n- `createOwnerTitleCasesCityWhenCityIsNew` \u2014 posts `\"gOtHaM cITY\"` (no existing owner there) and asserts the response `city` is `\"Gotham City\"`.\n- `createOwnerReusesExistingCitySpelling` \u2014 posts `\"MCFARLAND\"` (seed data has an owner in `\"McFarland\"`) and asserts the response `city` is `\"McFarland\"`, proving the existing non-title-case spelling is reused rather than flattened to `\"Mcfarland\"`.",
